❯ Write exactly one paragraph of about 90 words about lighthouses. Use no line breaks, no markdown, no lists. This instruction sentence is padded so the prompt itself is long enough to wrap: alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india
  juliet kilo lima mike.

⏺ Lighthouses have guided sailors along dangerous coastlines for centuries. Their powerful lamps flash distinctive patterns so that mariners can recognize specific stations at night and in fog. Early towers relied on open fires, while modern beacons
  use electric lights and automated systems that run with little human attention. Many lighthouses also marked hidden rocks, harbor entrances, and safe channels. Today, satellite navigation has reduced their practical role, yet many remain treasured
  landmarks that draw visitors and photographers. They stand as quiet reminders of human courage and the long effort to keep ships safe.

